Using loop
- name: Install packages
  hosts: all
  become: yes

  tasks:
    - name: Install package
      ansible.builtin.package:
        name: "{{ item }}"
        state: present
      loop:
        - nginx
        - git
        - vim
        - wget
How it works

The loop gives each package one by one to item:
loop
 ↓
nginx → item → install nginx
 ↓
git   → item → install git
 ↓
vim   → item → install vim
 ↓
wget  → item → install wget

So:

name: "{{ item }}"
means:  Use the current value from the loop as the package name.

But loop is not required here
You can simply do:
name:
  - nginx
  - git
  - vim
  - wget

This is usually simpler for package installation.
Loop is useful when you specifically need to perform the same task repeatedly for different values.
