when condition

In Ansible, a when condition means:

Run a task only when a particular condition is true.

Simple example
- name: Install nginx
  hosts: all
  become: yes

  tasks:
    - name: Install nginx
      yum:
        name: nginx
        state: present
      when: ansible_os_family == "RedHat"

Here:  when: ansible_os_family == "RedHat"
means:
Is this server RedHat?
       |
   Yes ↓ No
       |   \
    Run    Skip

So if you have:

Server 1 → RHEL
Server 2 → Ubuntu
Server 3 → RHEL

Ansible does:
Server 1 → condition true  → install nginx
Server 2 → condition false → skip
Server 3 → condition true  → install nginx


Another example
- name: Start nginx
  service:
    name: nginx
    state: started
  when: nginx_enabled == true

The task runs only when nginx_enabled is true.
